# Feature Audit: Observability, Runtime Events, and Artifacts

## 1. Scope

This audit covers observability APIs, runtime events, trace propagation, OpenTelemetry support, cost/SLO/incident data, artifacts, attestations, and evaluation readiness. It inspects `product_platform/observability`, `product_platform/runtime`, `product_platform/artifacts`, Tool Gateway runtime audit, Agent OS observability module, frontend observability pages, docs, and the Python SDK. Relevant benchmarks are LangSmith tracing/evaluation, AWS AgentCore Observability, Google ADK traces/evals, CrewAI tracing/OTel export, OpenTelemetry GenAI semantic conventions, and Phoenix/Braintrust/Galileo-style eval loops. Out of scope: compliance evidence export, covered in AUD.

## 2. Current Implementation Summary

Product observability routes start around `packages/product-platform/src/product_platform/api/app.py:11451` and focus on SLO objectives, cost events, incidents, chaos experiments, and rollouts. Frontend API types live in `frontend/src/api/observability.ts`, and UI in `frontend/src/features/observability/ObservabilityPage.tsx`. Runtime models expose sessions/actions with latency and correlation IDs. Tool Gateway runtime events are appended in `tool_gateway/runtime_audit.py`. Artifacts live in `product_platform/artifacts/repository.py` and artifact attestations in `0049_artifact_attestations.up.sql`. Agent OS has an alpha observability module under `packages/agent-os/modules/observability`.

Current workflow: operators can manually ingest SLO/cost/incident data, view dashboards, and inspect some runtime/action records. The system does not yet expose a first-class trace/run/span/eval model or W3C trace propagation across SDK, API, Tool Gateway, runtime, and artifacts.

